-- title:
--   Integrality modulo a prime over a henselian base
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a noetherian henselian local ring whose maximal ideal is principal, generated by an element $\varpi$, and let $S$ be a noetherian local ring. Let $\varphi : A[X] \to S$ be a ring homomorphism which is essentially of finite type, and assume: the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by the two elements $\varphi(\varpi)$ and $\varphi(X)$ (writing $\varphi(a)$ for the image of the constant polynomial $a$); the element $\varphi(\varpi)$ is prime in $S$; and there is a ring homomorphism $\chi_0 : S \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ onto the residue field of $A$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $S$ and which sends $\varphi(a)$ to the residue class of $a$ for every $a \in A$. Then for every prime element $p$ of $S$ that is not associated to $\varphi(\varpi)$, and for every $x \in S$, there exists a monic polynomial $r \in A[X]$ such that $p$ divides the value at $x$ of the polynomial obtained from $r$ by pushing its coefficients along $a \mapsto \varphi(a)$; that is, $p \mid r(x)$ in $S$.
--
--   This is a henselian form of the statement that a quasi-finite local algebra essentially of finite type over a henselian base is finite, here in the concrete shape that every element of $S$ is integral over $A$ modulo a prime $p$ not associated to $\varpi$, so that $S/(p)$ is integral over $A$. It is used in the analysis of stalks at smooth points in the theory of regular prolongations of algebraic curves, via [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smoothPointStalk_algebraicBlock_of_formallyEtale_of_henselian`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smoothPointStalk_algebraicBlock_of_formallyEtale_of_henselian); the proof combines the finiteness of localisations at maximal ideals of module-finite algebras over a henselian local ring with an approximation of arbitrary elements of $S$ by polynomial expressions in $\varphi(X)$ modulo the ideal $(p, \varphi(\varpi))$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HenselianLocalRing_forall_exists_monic_dvd_eval_of_prime_of_not_associated.lean

